These assignment-only files select one strict optimization lane.  They do not
contain package fingerprints, ABI identities, generation IDs, or profile paths.
Those machine-specific values belong in generated Portage policy outside Git.

PGO mode files may be layered with bolt-capture-ready.conf or bolt-deploy.conf.
GCC BOLT lanes must additionally include bolt-gcc-ready.conf.  Active modes fail
unless the global bashrc receives an exact fingerprint, ABI, compiler lane, and
all profile identity inputs required by that mode.

The ordinary make.conf and fallback environments contain no sample-profile or
BOLT readiness metadata.  The dispatcher is the sole owner of these stage sets:

* profile-map-ready: Clang line tables, profiling debug identity, unique
  internal linkage names, pseudo probes, and exactly one SHA-1 GNU build ID;
* BOLT capture/deploy for Clang: line tables, emitted relocations, and exactly
  one SHA-1 GNU build ID;
* BOLT capture/deploy for GCC: minimal line information, emitted relocations,
  exactly one SHA-1 GNU build ID, and disabled block partitioning;
* BOLT capture/deploy for Rust: target-only line information, emitted
  relocations, and exactly one SHA-1 GNU build ID.

Go readiness does not receive C/C++ or Rust flags; the exact package-produced
ELF remains subject to the fail-closed artifact classifier.
